# Previewing policy impact on the Meridian slice, before anything ships.
# kind, stock Sveltos v1.15.0, ConfigHub v0.6.5, 2026-09-28. The sandbox is a
# separate kind cluster (Kubernetes v1.35) that holds the policies and nothing
# else; every verdict below is its API server's own, from a server-side dry run.
# The policies are in policies/: replica-limits (a replica ceiling per class:
# test 4, uat 3, prod 5) and disallow-latest-tag, with the candidates in
# policies/candidates/. See docs/user/policy-checks.md.
#
# For case 1, a proposal was made at the root and promoted into the class bases
# only, so that each cluster's next promotion would bring it. Nothing was
# released. After the preview it was aborted and taken back out (case 5).
#
# During the recording: deleting a ValidatingAdmissionPolicy left the parameters
# its successors read stale until the sandbox's API server restarted, so
# `cub sveltos impact` now applies policies in place, and the sandbox was
# restarted before this run.

== 0. The proposal: 6 admission controller replicas at the root, promoted into the class bases only
$ cub function set --space mer-kyverno-base --unit kyverno --change-desc "Proposal: 6 admission controller replicas" -- set-yq '(select(.kind == "Deployment" and .metadata.name == "kyverno-admission-controller") | .spec.replicas) = 6'
$ cub changeorder create --space mer-kyverno-base six-replicas --change-workflow mer-kyverno-base/rollout
ok
$ cub variant promote --change-order mer-kyverno-base/six-replicas --target-stage bases --squash
Failed: no response body from server for req 
-- class-test admission replicas at head: 6
-- class-uat admission replicas at head: 2
-- class-prod admission replicas at head: 3

== 1. Application to policies: the root's proposal (6 admission controller replicas, promoted into the class bases only) against each cluster's own policies
$ cub sveltos impact --sandbox-kubeconfig sandbox.kubeconfig --component mer-kyverno --policy policies/replica-limits.yaml --policy policies/disallow-latest-tag.yaml --next
policies in force: policies/replica-limits.yaml, policies/disallow-latest-tag.yaml

TARGET            STAGE  CONFIG                                           OBJECT                                   NOW      THEN    VERDICT       WHY
eu-central-test1  test   kyverno@10 -> mer-kyverno-class-test/kyverno@13  Deployment kyverno-admission-controller  allowed  denied  newly denied  replica-limits (binding replica-limits-test): replicas 6 is above the ceiling of 4 for this class

1 newly denied, 0 newly allowed, 23 unchanged, 0 unknown

